custom-kernel/7.2.6/
  MT8163 kernel support for the Echo Show 5 (cronos), based on the linux-mtk
  mt8163/7.0 branch and adapted to Linux 7.2.6. The platform patch retains
  upstream copyright and license notices; patches/ and config/ contain the
  board adaptations under the licenses declared in each file.

  wifi-amazon/ is a pinned submodule of
  https://github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mt76x8-wifi.
  Its dual GPLv2/BSD notices remain in the upstream source headers.

  sources/amazon-kernel/ is a pinned submodule of
  https://github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mt8163.
  It supplies vendor codec build inputs and hardware reference sources under
  their upstream licenses. Local adaptations are stored separately as patches.

  initramfs/firmware/ contains the regulatory database with its ISC notice,
  MT7668 Bluetooth firmware, FPGA bitstreams, and the amplifier configuration.
  Device-specific boot images, bootloader dumps, and rescue archives are local
  build inputs and are not included in the source changes.
